WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.588
Your app already knows how to search, select, and get things done.

00:00:05.588 --> 00:00:09.404
What if an agent could use those same actions?

00:00:09.404 --> 00:00:10.676
Meet Fabrials UI.

00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:13.662
Start with a familiar interface.

00:00:13.662 --> 00:00:16.642
Filter the project list, then select a row.

00:00:16.642 --> 00:00:20.368
Every action stays visible, and the user stays in control.

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:24.794
Now call the same action as a structured tool.

00:00:24.794 --> 00:00:30.284
The arguments are validated, the table updates, and the result tells you exactly what changed.

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:35.499
Web MCP exposes those tools inside the browser.

00:00:35.499 --> 00:00:38.573
Native access needs experimental browser support.

00:00:38.573 --> 00:00:41.647
The manual interface keeps working everywhere.

00:00:42.766 --> 00:00:47.055
For remote MCP servers, connect, discover tools, and run them.

00:00:47.055 --> 00:00:52.630
Inspect the response, follow progress, and ask for input when it is needed.

00:00:53.733 --> 00:00:57.267
Install just the components you need with Bun.

00:00:57.267 --> 00:00:59.035
You own the code.

00:00:59.035 --> 00:01:00.360
Build for people.

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:02.569
Make it ready for agents.

00:01:02.569 --> 00:01:03.453
Fabrials UI.

